   $q$What can Nadia most reasonably conclude from watching Marcus before she decides?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He wants her to keep playing so that she can win the match.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He is tired and will probably agree to a draw of his own soon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"His game is likely going badly, so a sure half point matters more.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He is about to win, so her own result no longer matters at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His game is likely going badly, so a sure half point matters more.$q$, $q$The narrator says his hands pressed to his cheeks is "what he did when he was losing," so his half of the match is in danger. That makes a guaranteed half point on her board more valuable, not less.$q$, 'draft', '37cd2a2f-789d-5ae3-882f-1bcb1ddcd067')
