   $q$Why does Kenji's backup station suddenly become important?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mrs. Abernathy did not trust the finish camera's results.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Kenji's watches were the most accurate timers at the meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The finish camera had stopped working and missed the 800 meters.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The two runners asked to have their race timed again by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The finish camera had stopped working and missed the 800 meters.$q$, $q$Mrs. Abernathy finds "a frozen image of an empty track," so the camera missed the race and only hand times remain. The training sheet says hand times can be off by tenths, so they are not the most accurate timers.$q$, 'draft', 'af5efd6f-5f04-5752-b0f7-8613cd7984a3')
