   $q$According to the passage, how do the stakes show how much ice has melted?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The stakes change color as they are exposed to sunlight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The stakes sink deeper into the ice as the glacier warms.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"The stakes lean farther downhill as the glacier moves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"More of each pole shows above the surface as ice melts.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$More of each pole shows above the surface as ice melts.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says, "The more pole showing, the more ice had melted away around it." Stake 9's fall is a special case, not the normal way the stakes record melt.$q$, 'draft', '03ef8cd6-7294-5fa9-ad99-a5bca140ce10')
