   $q$Which evidence best supports the inference that the result at Stake 9 is surprising, not just one more data point?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Anjali hesitated before suggesting that they record two meters.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"Dr. Eze photographed the fallen stake from three different angles.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"Lower stakes showed at most two meters and higher ones under one, yet 9 exceeded two.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The stake was half buried in gritty snow with its base pointing downhill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lower stakes showed at most two meters and higher ones under one, yet 9 exceeded two.$q$, $q$The other stakes follow a pattern of less melt higher up, so a stake above Stake 8 losing more than two meters breaks the pattern. Photographing it shows care with an unusual case but does not by itself show the result breaks a pattern.$q$, 'draft', '03ef8cd6-7294-5fa9-ad99-a5bca140ce10')
